Thanks for your feedback. The cached token content is incorrectly truncated when output. I will fix it.

```cpp
if (cached_token.size() >= 3)
{
	float t_cost_ms = t_cost.cost();
	float token_per_sec = token_ids.size() / (t_cost_ms / 1000);
	auto tmp_out = tokenizer->Decode(cached_token);
	printf("tmp_out: %s\n", tmp_out.c_str());
	_attr.runing_callback(cached_token.data(), cached_token.size(), tmp_out.c_str(), token_per_sec, _attr.reserve);
	cached_token.clear();
}
```

This problem can be avoided by changing "if (cached_token.size() >= 3)" to "if (cached_token.size() >= 5)".
